The Java and Kotlin half of the TaffyGo string catalogue.

Grit turns this into `values-<locale>/taffy_android_strings.xml`, which the
Android resource pipeline compiles into `R.string.*`. That output shape is why
this is a separate .grd from `taffy_strings.grd`: the pak half is read by
browser-process C++ and the two never carry the same message twice.

There is exactly one shipping locale today. PAR-L10N-001 requires English UI
with every string externalized and pseudo-localization tested; the launch
language set beyond English is `[Open (OD-060)]`, so `<translations>` below is
empty rather than listing .xtb files that do not exist. Empty is the honest
state and it is one line to change when OD-060 lands.

VERIFY AT SP-01: the pseudo-locale build path at the pinned milestone — the
`enable_pseudolocales` GN argument, the `ar-XB` and `en-XA` entries in
build/config/locales.gni, and whether grit generates them for an `android`
output type. Upstream files to read: build/config/locales.gni and
tools/grit/grit/pseudolocales.py. Independently of that answer, the
host-runnable check in tools/check_strings.py already pseudo-localizes this
catalogue and asserts the properties that matter; the GN argument only decides
whether a device build can also *show* it.
-->
<!-- `output_all_resource_defines` is deliberately absent: grit at milestone
     152 removed the attribute and fails the parse on encountering it. This
     file carried it from an older grit reference before any checkout
     existed to test against. -->
<grit latest_public_release="0" current_release="1"
      source_lang_id="en"
      enc_check="möl">
  <outputs>
    <output filename="values/taffy_android_strings.xml" type="android" lang="en" />
  </outputs>
  <translations>
    <!-- Empty until OD-060 sets the launch languages. Each language added
         here needs its own quality evidence (PAR-L10N-003). -->
  </translations>
  <release seq="1" allow_pseudo="true">
    <messages fallback_to_english="true">
      <part file="strings/taffy_download_strings.grdp" />
    </messages>
  </release>
</grit>
